     ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"/nostr/relays/nips/nip-11/"},"children":["NIP-11"]},"\n            ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"/nostr/relays/research-atlas/"},"children":["Sources"]},"\n          "]},"\n        "]},"\n      "]},"\n    "]},"\n\n    ",{"tag":"section","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-main"},"children":["\n      ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-shell crays-article-layout"},"children":["\n        ",{"tag":"aside","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-toc","aria-label":"Reading path"},"children":["\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Reading path"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#infrastructure-has-a-bill"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["01"]},"Infrastructure has a bill"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#payment-changes-the-power-shape"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["02"]},"Payment changes the power shape"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#spam-is-an-economic-problem-too"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["03"]},"Spam is an economic problem too"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#business-models-need-exit"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["04"]},"Business models need exit"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"#what-belongs-in-the-market-map"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["05"]},"What belongs in the market map"]},"\n        "]},"\n        ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-content"},"children":["\n          ",{"tag":"header","attributes":{"className":"crays-nostr-article-masthead"},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"crays-nostr-article-masthead__meta"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["Relays"]},{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["407 words"]},{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["Relay economics"]}]},"\n            ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"className":"crays-nostr-article-masthead__title"},"children":["Paid Relays and the Economics of Keeping Nostr Usable"]},"\n            ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{"className":"crays-nostr-article-masthead__deck"},"children":["Free public relays keep the network approachable, but serious reliability eventually needs funding, policy and operator incentives."]},"\n          "]},"\n          ",{"tag":"aside","attributes":{"className":"crays-nostr-source-card","aria-label":"Quick read"},"children":[{"tag":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["The quick read"]},{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["Use this when a paid relay feels against the spirit of Nostr. Payment can reduce spam and fund operations, but it also creates access rules. The serious question is not free versus paid. It is what each relay promises, what it costs and how easily you can leave."]}]},"\n          ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"infrastructure-has-a-bill"},"children":["Infrastructure has a bill"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Nostr can make identity portable, but it cannot make servers free. Relays need bandwidth, storage, monitoring, updates and human attention. Public relays often begin as generosity. Some survive that way. Many eventually face spam, cost or burnout."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Paid relays make the cost visible. They can fund better uptime, reduce spam through admission and give operators a reason to maintain the service. That can be healthy, as long as the payment model is clear and the user can still choose other relays."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"payment-changes-the-power-shape"},"children":["Payment changes the power shape"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["A paid relay is not automatically more trustworthy. It has incentives, support expectations and access rules. It may offer better service, but it may also become a gate. A user who pays can feel entitled to persistence. An operator who charges may need policies, refunds, moderation and legal boundaries."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["That is not a flaw. It is the point where infrastructure becomes a service. The hub should say that plainly instead of pretending every relay is a neutral commons."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"spam-is-an-economic-problem-too"},"children":["Spam is an economic problem too"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Open relays invite abuse. If writing is free and identity is cheap to create, spam can consume bandwidth and attention. Rate limits, proof-of-work, payments, authentication and reputation are all attempts to make abuse more expensive without making normal use unbearable."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The best relay design is honest about tradeoffs. A relay that filters nothing may be ideologically clean and operationally useless. A relay that filters too much may become a platform gate. Paid access is one tool in that spectrum."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"business-models-need-exit"},"children":["Business models need exit"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["A paid relay should not become a trap. You should know what happens if you stop paying, whether old events remain readable, how to export or republish important data, what terms apply and whether another relay can serve the same role."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["This is where Nostr's architecture helps. Because the identity is the key and events can be copied, payment for a relay does not have to mean surrender. But the product has to support that exit path in practice."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"what-belongs-in-the-market-map"},"children":["What belongs in the market map"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["A useful market page should separate public defaults, paid relays, local relays, search relays, wallet relays, directory relays and experimental software. It should show the claim and the source, not just a logo."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["When you compare relays, ask what you are buying or receiving: reach, durability, filtering, speed, privacy posture, community context, support or software tooling. Those are different products hiding behind the same word."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"sources-worth-opening"},"children":["Sources worth opening"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Open these when you want the standard, implementation, monitor or operator trail behind the page."]},"\n          ",{"tag":"ul","attributes":{},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"https://nostr.watch/","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer noopener"},"children":["Nostr Watch"]}]},"\n            ",{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"https://nostr.co.uk/relays/","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer noopener"},"children":["nostr.co.uk relay list"]}]},"\n            ",{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"https://nostr.wine/","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer noopener"},"children":["nostr.wine"]}]},"\n            ",{"tag":"li","attributes":{},"children":[{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"https://relay.nostr.net/","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer noopener"},"children":["relay.nostr.net"]}]},"\n          "]},"\n          ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"useful-next-pages"},"children":["Useful next pages"]},"\n          ",{"tag":"nav","attributes":{"className":"crays-nostr-apps-ecosystem-nav","aria-label":"Related Relay routes"},"children":[{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"/nostr/relays/field-guide/paid-relays/"},"children":["Paid relay field guide"]},{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"/nostr/relays/nip-42-relay-auth/"},"chi